<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad bin Rashid Al Mualla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad bin Rashid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mualla">Al Mualla</a> was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umm-al-quwain">Umm al-Quwain</a>, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trucial-states">Trucial States</a>, from 1929 to 1981. His long rule spanned the period of British protection and the founding of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>, which Umm al-Quwain joined in December 1971. He was succeeded by his son Rashid bin Ahmad Al Mualla.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-bin-rashid-al-mualla.jpg" alt="Ahmad bin Rashid Al Mualla" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ulises Icardi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_jeque_Ahmad_bin_Rashid_Al_Mualla_(1902-1981)_fue_gobernante_del_emirato_de_Umm_Al_Quwain_desde_1928_hasta_1981.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
